# Time flies in Russian: идёт дождь, тебе идёт
subtitle: "Идёт дождь, время летит, тебе идёт: Russian motion verbs where nobody moves, the day Masha comes back from Sochi."
tags: ["russian","идёт дождь","verbs of motion","russian idioms","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/verbs-of-motion","phrases/idioms"]
thumb: "band \"Nobody is walking\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Reading Pushkin in Russian: The Blizzard","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/200-russian-pushkin-blizzard.cast"}

